\[ V_{\text{half}} = \frac{1}{2} \times 432\pi = 216\pi \]

Using the approximation \(\pi \approx 3.14159\), we can calculate the numerical value:

\[ V_{\text{half}} \approx 216 \times 3.14159 = 678.58464 \]

Rounding this to one decimal place, we get:

\[ V_{\text{half}} \approx 678.6 \]

Therefore, the volume of the half cylinder is \(\boxed{678.6}\) cubic centimeters.
