\[ A_{\text{larger base}} = \pi R^2 = \pi \times 4^2 = 16\pi \]

The area of the smaller base is:
\[ A_{\text{smaller base}} = \pi r^2 = \pi \times 2^2 = 4\pi \]

The total surface area of the solid is the sum of the lateral surface area of the frustum, the lateral surface area of the smaller cone, and the areas of the two bases:
